.Dd November 11, 2026
.Dt MMIO_CREATE 2
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm mmio_create
.Nd create a device-memory region
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Fn mmio_create root_dev phys len attrs
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm creates an
.Em MmioRegion
capability for the device window at physical address
.Fa phys
of
.Fa len
bytes.
.Fa root_dev
must be the
.Em RootDevice
capability (well-known handle 3 of the first process) or a duplicate that
keeps the
.Dv ADMIN
right; any other handle, or one without
.Dv ADMIN ,
fails with
.Er EPERM .
.Bl -bullet
.It
.Fa phys
and
.Fa len
must be non-zero multiples of 4096.
.It
The range must not intersect ordinary RAM, the kernel image, loader memory,
or the local APIC / IOAPIC windows the kernel owns; such ranges fail with
.Er EPERM .
Ranges inside
.Em Reserved
or
.Em Mmio
memory-map regions, or outside the memory map, are device space and allowed.
.It
.Fa attrs
is reserved; only 0 is accepted
.Er EINVAL
otherwise.
.El
The returned handle carries
.Dv READ ,
.Dv WRITE ,
.Dv MAP ,
.Dv DUP
and
.Dv TRANSFER .
.Pp
The region is mapped with
.Xr map 2
using the memory-object conventions: offset and length must be page aligned
and stay inside the region, otherwise
.Er EINVAL .
The mapping is uncached (x86-64 PCD+PWT cache-disable + write-through, the
same attribute pair the kernel uses for its own device windows), never
executable, and exists only in the mapped process; it is removed on process
exit without recycling the device pages.
A writable mapping requires the
.Dv WRITE
right.
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Er EPERM
No root capability with
.Dv ADMIN ,
or the range is not device space.
.It Er EINVAL
Misaligned or overflowing addresses, zero length, or unknown attributes.
.It Er EMFILE
The process handle table is full.
.El
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD ABI v1.
